==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Hippoe]]s spawn after 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>, delay 2~16.67 seconds<sup>60f~500f</sup>.
*3 [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 6~16.67 seconds<sup>180f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 24 seconds<sup>720f</sup>, delay 20~33.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Sir Metal Seal]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**3 [[Super Metal Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Once the boss appears, have as many [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] out as [[Sir Metal Seal]] is a very tough enemy and often takes a lot of [[Critical Hit]]s to take out. The enemy base will continuously spawn Super Metal Hippoes, so take care of some of the enemies quickly so you won't be swarmed. Bring a [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attacker]] like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] to help take out the Hippoes hiding behind the Metal enemies. Most Critical Hitters will work, with [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] (must be in [[True Form]] to outrange Super Metal Hippoe and Sir Metal Seal), [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Major Space Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]] being some of the more accessible options.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] that has a [[Special Abilities|special ability]] targeting [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies and/or can do [[Critical Hit]]s at a decent chance will be good here. Listed below are more specified examples of good Ubers to use in this stage.
*[[Marauder Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Marauder Cat]]: Just like most other stages full of [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies, Marauder Cat makes this stage a joke as long as he is in his Evolved/[[True Form]].
*[[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]]: An even better option, Hayabusa can destroy most if not all of the Metal enemies in this stage with his powerful, Long Distance strikes.
*[[Graveflower Verbena (Uber Rare Cat)|Graveflower Verbena]]: Another Critical-Hitting Uber, her multi-hits increase her chance of doing a Critical Hit on the Metal enemies here.
*[[Princess Kaguya (Uber Rare Cat)|Princess Kaguya]]: Great [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control]] that can slow both the Heavenly Hippoes and Metal enemies themselves, outranging them all. It's recommended to use her Normal Form over her Evolved/True Form for spammability, since there are no enemies that outrange her.
*[[Sakura Sonic (Uber Rare Cat)|Sakura Sonic]]: Great crowd-controller for all the Metal enemies here and has a chance to do a Critical Hit.

